      "created_at": "2017-07-01T00:56:39.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ameena\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/48/1907_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ameena:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>What is he doing when he unleashes the damage? Pulling them out from under said rock, crushing them into a ball and chucking them at something? <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/smiley.png?v=12\" title=\":smiley:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":smiley:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Actually… We tend to use the rock more as a repository for stuff we want to get out of the villain’s play. (“Oh, the Mask of the Matriarch again. That’s going under the rock!”) So it doesn’t really come up all that often!</p>",
